# [#](#scatter-chart) Scatter Chart

Scatter charts are based on basic line charts with the x-axis changed to a linear axis. To use a scatter chart, data must be passed as objects containing X and Y properties. The example below creates a scatter chart with 4 points.

config
setup

const config = {
type: 'scatter',
data: data,
options: {
scales: {
x: {
type: 'linear',
position: 'bottom'
}
}
}
};

```
const config = {
  type: 'scatter',
  data: data,
  options: {
    scales: {
      x: {
        type: 'linear',
        position: 'bottom'
      }
    }
  }
};
```

const data = {
datasets: [{
label: 'Scatter Dataset',
data: [{
x: -10,
y: 0
}, {
x: 0,
y: 10
}, {
x: 10,
y: 5
}, {
x: 0.5,
y: 5.5
}],
backgroundColor: 'rgb(255, 99, 132)'
}],
};

```
const data = {
  datasets: [{
    label: 'Scatter Dataset',
    data: [{
      x: -10,
      y: 0
    }, {
